I read the manifest references (§2–§4, §7–§8, §10, §10a, §12, §15) first. Values in ‹…› come from the backlog or command output at run time. `SCR` is my scratch root and `REPO=~/work/ccs.ansible`.

I take your word that acceptance was WireGuard's last gate. If its backlog row lists a `ccs-ops` rollout, that is the release and goes to the operator as a poll.

## 1. Look before touching (Bash, foreground)

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
herdr agent list
git -C "$REPO" fetch origin && git -C "$REPO" rev-parse origin/main
git -C "$REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive" status --porcelain   # must be empty
git -C "$REPO" branch --merged origin/main | grep -F feat/wg-keepalive-relay
ps -p 48211 -o pid,command                                         # still my codex app-server?
codex plugin list | grep -i superpowers; claude plugin list | grep -i superpowers
```

If superpowers is missing from either CLI, I poll the operator to install it. I use no substitute.

## 2. Backlog (Edit, foreground `bash build-backlog.sh`, Artifact update)

I save the pasted ping summary and "accepted" to `$SCR/evidence/‹wg›/acceptance.txt`, then write two rows:

| Task | Status | Owner | Next step | Docs closed |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| ‹wg› WireGuard keepalive relay | `docs closed` | main | docs PR, then cleanup | no: snapshot, living docs, memory |
| ‹rdp› RDP audio | `brainstorm` | `prod-codex`, `prod-fable` | round 1 drafts | no |

## 3. Two new product-advisor tabs (Bash, foreground)

```bash
mkdir -p "$SCR/brainstorm/‹rdp›-rdp-audio" "$SCR/inbox" "$SCR/briefs"
P=$(herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd "$SCR/brainstorm" --label prod-codex --no-focus | jq -r .result.root_pane.pane_id)
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane "$P" --timeout 120000 -- \
  -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
P=$(herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd "$SCR/brainstorm" --label prod-fable --no-focus | jq -r .result.root_pane.pane_id)
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane "$P" --timeout 120000 -- \
  --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```

## 4. Round-1 brief (Write two files, then two background Bash calls)

```
You are product advisor ‹A|B› in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       ‹rdp› — RDP audio
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file exists and you have reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go."
FACTS      repo ~/work/ccs.ansible, main @ ‹sha›, includes PR #165 (WireGuard keepalive
           relay). Canary site ccs-it runs that main (re-run changed=0); ccs-ops does not.
           UNVERIFIED, not a fact: the task touches the desktop and gateway roles.
DECIDED    ‹the applicable hard rules of CLAUDE.md, byte for byte›; deploy only from merged
           main, canary ccs-it first; "by morning" shortens no round and waives no gate
READ       nothing from the other advisor in this round
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      $SCR/brainstorm/‹rdp›-rdp-audio/draft-‹codex|fable›.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   45 min to the first report; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

```bash
# background, one call per tab (same for prod-fable)
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat "$SCR/briefs/‹rdp›-r1-codex.txt")" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$SCR/inbox/prod-codex.last"
```

## 5. Status to the operator

This is in Russian per the §15 ruling; the rest of my answer is in English because this session requires it.

> **Сейчас**
> - WireGuard keepalive relay (‹wg›): приёмка записана — ваш ping без потерь (0 %) и «accepted». Задача ещё не `done`: закрываю документацию (снимок состояния ccs-it, рабочие документы, статус дизайна и плана) и убираю за собой — вкладка `wgka`, её worktree (отдельная рабочая копия репозитория), ветка, вспомогательный процесс `codex app-server`.
> - RDP audio (‹rdp›): задача в бэклоге со статусом `brainstorm`. Два продуктовых советника (Codex gpt-6-astra и Claude Fable 5.1, новые отдельные вкладки) получили задание на независимые черновики — ещё работают, результата нет.
>
> **Дальше**: перекрёстная критика, общий документ, утверждение голосующими советниками (2/2). Утверждённый дизайн опубликую на русском как Artifact. «К утру» — срок, а не сокращение процесса: брейншторм идёт полностью. Если полный цикл не успевает или голоса разойдутся, придёт опрос и будет ждать вас.
>
> **От вас**: сейчас ничего. Если понадобится факт, известный только вам, придёт опрос — вероятнее всего в ближайшие 20–30 минут.
>
> **Проверено**: PR #165 в `main`; мой повторный прогон на ccs-it — `changed=0`; связь — по вашему ping (ваше свидетельство, не моё измерение). **Не проверено**: по RDP audio — ничего.
> **Живые машины**: ccs-it — развёрнут `main` с PR #165; ccs-ops — без изменений.
> **Решения голосования с прошлого статуса**: ‹id бюллетеней или «нет»›. **Бэклог**: ‹ссылка›

In short: acceptance is recorded, WireGuard close-out is under way, the RDP audio brainstorm is running in full, and the operator has nothing to do now.

## 6. Close WireGuard while round 1 runs

**Closing report from `wgka`** (after `herdr agent get wgka` shows `focused: false`; Bash, background, `--timeout 600000`, same recipe):

```
Task ‹wg› is merged (PR #165), deployed to the canary and accepted. Closing phase, this task
only. Reply in English. Do not edit, commit or push. Report, compact: (1) output of
`git status --porcelain` and `git log -1 --oneline`; (2) living docs this change makes stale,
by path; (3) non-obvious traps or mechanisms you verified in roles gateway and host_proxy,
each with evidence (path:line or command output). No proposals for other tasks.
```

**Docs worktree** (Bash, foreground):

```bash
git -C "$REPO" worktree add "$REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs" -b chore/wg-keepalive-docs-close origin/main
```

**Prose subagent** (Agent tool, Sonnet, background):

```
Reply in English. Documentation only; no decisions, no host access. Work only in
‹absolute path›/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs. From $SCR/evidence/‹wg›/ and
$SCR/inbox/wgka.last: update projects/ccs/soul/‹ccs-it hosts›.md to what the evidence shows
and nothing more (ccs-ops unchanged); update the living docs listed; mark the design and plan
docs "implemented — PR #165, merge ‹sha›". No session links. Do not commit. Report the files
changed and, per claim, the evidence line it rests on.
```

I check every claim against the evidence and run the project's docs-only check. Then I commit, push, open the PR and merge it with `gh pr merge ‹n› --merge --delete-branch`. It is docs-only, so there is no ballot; I report it in the next status.

**Cleanup** (Bash, foreground):

```bash
herdr tab close ‹wgka tab_id›
git -C "$REPO" worktree remove "$REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive"
git -C "$REPO" worktree remove "$REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs"
git -C "$REPO" worktree prune
git -C "$REPO" branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs-close
git -C "$REPO" pull && git -C "$REPO" worktree list
kill 48211        # only after step 1 confirmed it is my broker; advisor Codex processes stay
```

I never use `--force`. Then I write two memory notes with `MEMORY.md` pointers: `wg-keepalive-relay-lessons` (the verified traps) and `rdp-audio-brainstorm-state` (tabs, paths, round). The WireGuard row becomes `done` and I republish.

## 7. Voting advisors (both idle, no ballot open)

I run `herdr agent read adv-codex --source visible` and the same for `adv-fable`. At 50% or more context used, I send in the background `/compact` to Codex and `/compact mid-task: keep the protocol.md path and revision, every ballot result and adopted concern, and the open items` to Fable. Then I ask each for a one-line status.

## 8. On each notification

- I read `inbox/‹name›.last`, then run `herdr agent get`.
- I answer facts with evidence and answer `prod-fable`'s permission prompts myself, default deny.
- Every real choice becomes a neutral ballot sent to both voters at once.
- Rounds 2 and 3 are relayed by path, followed by the design-approval ballot.
- On 2/2 the row becomes `brainstormed` and the Russian Artifact and a status go out. No executor is created before that.

## Why

RDP audio is a new task, so it enters at stage 0: a backlog entry, two product advisors from two model families, then 2/2 approval. "Go" starts that. "By morning" is a wish that shortens no round and waives no gate. The full cycle can plausibly finish overnight because the vote owns every design question, so there is nothing to poll yet. If that changes, the operator gets the slip-or-waive poll.

`wgka` is not reused. One tab is one task: its context is WireGuard working memory, and a second task would inherit its assumptions. No executor may exist before `brainstormed`, and one tab designing alone is what stage 0 replaces. Its knowledge survives as evidence-backed docs the advisors can read.

`adv-codex` and `adv-fable` do not draft, because a voter that drafted would judge its own work.

WireGuard is accepted, not done. `done` needs the docs checklist and the cleanup. Both run beside round 1, so they cost the deadline nothing.

I design nothing: the brief carries the operator's words and facts, with my one guess labelled unverified.

After nine hours, state lives in files, and the voter tabs are compacted while idle rather than mid-vote.
